Input: {"question": "Where is Chesapeake High School located?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d00", "start": 0, "end": 151, "text": "Chesapeake High School (Baltimore County) Chesapeake High School (CHS), is a four-year public high school in Baltimore County, Maryland, United States."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d00", "start": 152, "end": 288, "text": "Chesapeake High School is one of two high schools in Maryland by that name, the other being Chesapeake High School, Anne Arundel County."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d00", "start": 289, "end": 400, "text": "The Chesapeake High School of Baltimore County is located in southeast corner of the county in Essex, Maryland."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d00", "start": 401, "end": 539, "text": "The school borders the school districts of Kenwood High School, Sparrows Point High School, Dundalk High School, and Patapsco High School."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d00", "start": 540, "end": 593, "text": "Widely known for its Virtual Lab and MCJROTC program."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d00", "start": 594, "end": 617, "text": "The high school is on ."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d00", "start": 618, "end": 632, "text": "Chesapeake has"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d01", "start": 0, "end": 141, "text": "Chesapeake High School (Baltimore County) Chesapeake High School (CHS), is a four-year public high school in Orlando, Florida, United States."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d01", "start": 142, "end": 278, "text": "Chesapeake High School is one of two high schools in Maryland by that name, the other being Chesapeake High School, Anne Arundel County."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d01", "start": 279, "end": 383, "text": "The Chesapeake High School of Orlando is located in the southeast corner of the city in a suburban area."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d01", "start": 384, "end": 522, "text": "The school borders the school districts of Kenwood High School, Sparrows Point High School, Dundalk High School, and Patapsco High School."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d01", "start": 523, "end": 576, "text": "Widely known for its Virtual Lab and MCJROTC program."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d01", "start": 577, "end": 599, "text": "The high school is on."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d01", "start": 600, "end": 614, "text": "Chesapeake has"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d02", "start": 0, "end": 141, "text": "Chesapeake High School (Ohio) Chesapeake High School, commonly referred to locals as \"The Peake\" is a public high school in Chesapeake, Ohio."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d02", "start": 142, "end": 226, "text": "It is the only high school in the Chesapeake Union Exempted Village School District."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d02", "start": 227, "end": 329, "text": "Chesapeake's first high school was established in 1924 at what is now the Chesapeake Community Center."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d02", "start": 330, "end": 377, "text": "Their athletic teams' nickname is the Panthers."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d02", "start": 378, "end": 419, "text": "Their school colors are purple and white."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d02", "start": 420, "end": 538, "text": "They have football, basketball, baseball, softball, track and field, golf, soccer, volleyball, and wrestling programs."}, "D3S7": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d02", "start": 539, "end": 605, "text": "The athletic programs compete in the Ohio Valley Conference (OVC)."}, "D3S8": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d02", "start": 606, "end": 657, "text": "The principal of Chesapeake is Chris Smith, and the"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d03", "start": 0, "end": 17, "text": "“Bye Bye Birdie”."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d03", "start": 18, "end": 159, "text": "In October 2007, Chesapeake High School was listed as one of four high schools in Anne Arundel County that had outbreaks of staph infections."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d03", "start": 160, "end": 289, "text": "28 cases of the infection have also been reported at Severna Park High School, Glen Burnie High School, and Old Mill High School."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d03", "start": 290, "end": 577, "text": "In February 2008, Chesapeake parents began an organization (CEEDSS) to protest a special education program, known as CRP or the Chesapeake Regional Program, that has been in the school since 1990, but according to parents has been disruptive to education and concealed by administration."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d03", "start": 578, "end": 615, "text": "Sports teams at Chesapeake, with both"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d04", "start": 0, "end": 14, "text": ", Maryland ) ."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0481-ab574ac174f6:d04", "start": 15, "end": 579, "text": "Public high school in Pasadena , Maryland , United States Chesapeake High School Address 4798 Mountain Road Pasadena , Maryland United St